Description: firmware content analysis for secrets, SBOM, CVEs and licenses
 mithril analyzes the contents of firmware and IoT software, a single file or
 an unpacked rootfs, for four things as structured JSON: embedded secrets and
 key material; a software bill of materials (emitted as CycloneDX and SPDX)
 built from package databases, language manifests and binary version strings;
 known CVEs matched against a local offline vulnerability mirror; and
 open-source licenses.
 .
 It pairs with moria, which handles structural identification and unpacking.
 Secrets, SBOM and license analysis run fully offline. The CVE pass reads a
 local mirror that is refreshed out of band (mithril --fetch-db, which needs
 curl). Live verification of candidate secrets is delegated to trufflehog when
 it is installed; mithril never links it.
